#!/bin/sh

#
# recordctl - Enable/disable audio recording in the OpenBSD kernel
#
# CHANGE LOG:
#
# v0.1   - 2024-07-29 - Morgan Aldridge <morgant@makkintosshu.com>
#                       Initial version.
# v0.1.1 - 2024-08-10 - Morgan Aldridge
#                       Added Makefile and manual page.
# v0.1.2 - 2024-09-07 - Morgan Aldridge
#                       Require root.
# v0.2.0 - 2025-10-24 - Morgan Aldridge
#                       List audio/video record state by default, instead of
#                       toggling state.  Changed options for showing/setting
#                       audio & video record state from '-a' & '-v' to
#                       a control sytax like sysctl(8), mixerctl(8), and
#                       sndioctl(1). Added new '-a' option to show both audio
#                       and video record control states (now the default).
#                       Added new 'n' option to supress printing control
#                       name and only print value. Replaced use of echo
#                       with printf. Updated usage output.
# v0.3.0 - 2025-10-24 - Morgan Aldridge
#                       Implemented previously stubbed-out monitor mode,
#                       including new '-c' option for specifying the
#                       number of seconds between checks of applicable
#                       sysctl(8) variables. Improved error messages and
#                       warnings when incompatible options and arguments
#                       are combined. Only requires root privileges for set 
#                       and toggle functionality, not get or monitor.
#
# LICENSE:
#
# Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Morgan Aldridge
#
# Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
# of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
# in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
# to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
# copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
# furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:
